      "text": "The Maltese Falcon (1941) stands as the quintessential film noir, establishing conventions that would define the genre for decades to come. John Huston's directorial debut transforms Dashiell Hammett's hard-boiled novel into a masterpiece of shadow and cynicism. Humphrey Bogart's portrayal of Sam Spade created the template for the noir detective, while the film's intricate plot about greed and betrayal set the standard for crime dramas."
