    },
    {
      "type": "culturalContext",
      "text": "Released as America stood on the brink of World War II, the film captured a growing sense of moral ambiguity and societal paranoia. Its themes of trust and betrayal resonated with audiences facing global uncertainty. The character of Brigid O'Shaughnessy challenged traditional female roles in Hollywood, presenting a complex femme fatale who was both victim and manipulator."
    },
